The table assumes a cold capacity-two site per row.
The megamorphic state can use a shared lookup cache,
but shared entries still need all relevant keys and
validity checks. A long sequence of per-site guards can
cost more than the lookup it was supposed to avoid.
Gather counts before tuning thresholds; a cache that
turns megamorphic after several rare receiver classes
may miss the dominant phase of a workload.

